{
  "_comment": [
    "Booster + sustainer, flown by BOTH the engine we ship and pristine upstream core.",
    "",
    "The airframe mirrors ParityMain.runStagingScenario's 'timed' pattern - the",
    "high-power staging case: separation at booster burnout, sustainer lit by",
    "electronics 1 s later, booster recovering under its own chute on its own",
    "branch. That scenario is already locked across JVM/JS/WASM; what it has never",
    "been is compared to upstream.",
    "",
    "EVERY aero- or mass-relevant property is explicit, on purpose. A property left",
    "out would be supplied by each side's own default, and two engines agreeing",
    "because they share a default is not evidence while two disagreeing over",
    "different defaults is a false alarm. The one deliberate exception is a property",
    "where BOTH sides fall through to the same upstream component default and",
    "neither injects one of its own (fin cant, tube finish, chute material): those",
    "are upstream's value on both sides by construction.",
    "",
    "Nose cone 'shape' is the property that taught this: ComponentFactory defaults a",
    "missing shape to CONICAL while upstream's NoseCone constructor does not, so a",
    "fixture that omitted it would have compared two different rockets.",
    "",
    "Every component that can appear as an event SOURCE carries a 'name' for the",
    "same reason, and run.mjs fails if one does not. An unnamed component falls",
    "back to its type's default name, and the two sides render that differently ON",
    "PURPOSE: upstream translates it ('Inner Tube'), while the shipped engine",
    "installs a bare DebugTranslator so the kernel emits stable machine keys",
    "('[InnerTube.InnerTube]') for web/src/services/warningText.ts to localize -",
    "see the note on Application.getTranslator in src/shims. Naming the component",
    "sidesteps a difference that is deliberate, without weakening the comparison."
  ],

